Wazuh SIEM Deployment Summary

Overview

As part of the Graytech SOC Analyst Home Lab, I deployed a Wazuh SIEM server to collect, analyze, and monitor security events from Windows, Linux, and future lab systems.

The goal of this setup is to gain hands-on SOC analyst experience by collecting real endpoint and authentication telemetry, investigating alerts, and documenting security events in a realistic lab environment.

SIEM Platform

- SIEM: Wazuh
- Deployment Type: All-in-one installation
- Components Installed:
  - Wazuh Manager
  - Wazuh Indexer
  - Wazuh Dashboard
  - Filebeat

Server Role

The SIEM was deployed on a dedicated Ubuntu server instead of the main Windows workstation.

This design allows the Windows workstation and domain controller to act as monitored endpoints while the Ubuntu server acts as the centralized security monitoring platform.

Lab Network Role

Ubuntu Server
  - Wazuh Manager
  - Wazuh Indexer
  - Wazuh Dashboard
  - Local Wazuh monitoring agent

Windows Server / DC01
  - Planned Wazuh Agent
  - Active Directory security logs
  - Authentication events
  - Account management events

Main Windows Workstation
  - Planned Wazuh Agent
  - Endpoint security logs
  - Defender events
  - PowerShell logs
  - Sysmon telemetry

Router / Future Lab Networks
  - Planned syslog/network telemetry
  - Future subnet/VLAN monitoring


For the domain controller and Windows workstation, the lab will collect:

